.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt DTFL_COLLECTION_ARRANGE_BY_KEY 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_collection_arrange_by_key ,
.Nm dtfl_arranged_reduce_core ,
.Nm dtfl_arranged_reduce_abelian
.Nd arrange a keyed collection and reduce an arrangement directly
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/arrange.h
.In dtfl/reduce.h
.Ft dtfl_arranged *
.Fn dtfl_collection_arrange_by_key "dtfl_collection *c" "const dtfl_type *key" "const dtfl_type *val" "const char *name"
.Ft dtfl_arranged *
.Fn dtfl_arranged_reduce_core "dtfl_arranged *a" "const char *name" "const dtfl_type *out_val" "const dtfl_diff *out_diff" "dtfl_reduce_core_fn logic" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft dtfl_arranged *
.Fn dtfl_arranged_reduce_abelian "dtfl_arranged *a" "const char *name" "const dtfl_type *out_val" "const dtfl_diff *out_diff" "dtfl_reduce_core_fn logic" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn dtfl_collection_arrange_by_key
indexes a collection of
.No key Ns || Ns value
records by key.
Each record is split into its key and value by the length of
.Va key ,
the leading field, updates are exchanged by the key prefix so a join finds
matching keys on one worker, and the result trace indexes
.Pq key , value .
.Va val
describes the value side so the library can order and index values.
.Va name
labels the operator, or is
.Dv NULL
for the default.
The returned
.Vt dtfl_arranged
is the shared index that
.Xr dtfl_arranged_join_core 3 ,
.Fn dtfl_arranged_reduce_core
and
.Fn dtfl_arranged_reduce_abelian
read: the cost of indexing is paid once and shared.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_arranged_reduce_core
reduces an arrangement
.Va a
.Pq key to value
directly, producing an output arrangement
.Pq key to Va out_val , Va out_diff No differences .
For each key whose input or tentative output changes,
.Va logic
is called with the key, the accumulated input multiset and the tentative
accumulated output multiset, and emits the output change through the sink.
The input multiset is the
.Va n
pairs
.Pq Va in_vals Ns Bq i , Va in_diffs Ns Bq i ,
and the tentative output multiset is the
.Va m
pairs
.Pq Va out_vals Ns Bq i , Va out_diffs Ns Bq i .
The emitted pairs are the change to apply to the output, so a logic that
wants to keep the prior output must retract it itself.
.Va out_diff
need not be Abelian.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_arranged_reduce_abelian
is the same, but wraps
.Va logic
so that it retracts the prior output automatically
.Pq negates and appends the tentative output, then consolidates ,
so
.Va logic
need only produce the new output for each key.
.Va out_diff
must be Abelian.
.Pp
In both,
.Va a
is read, not consumed; the caller still owns it.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Each function returns a new
.Vt dtfl_arranged
handle the caller owns and frees with
.Xr dtfl_arranged_free 3 .
.Fn dtfl_collection_arrange_by_key
indexes
.Va c ;
the reduce functions produce an output arrangement over the reduced trace.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Arrange two keyed collections and equijoin them, then reduce one to a
per-key aggregate:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl_arranged *l = dtfl_collection_arrange_by_key(c1, u64, u64, "L");
dtfl_arranged *r = dtfl_collection_arrange_by_key(c2, u64, u64, "R");
dtfl_collection *j = dtfl_arranged_join_core(l, r, out, result, DTFL_NOCTX);

dtfl_arranged *a = dtfl_collection_arrange_by_key(c, u64, u64, "A");
dtfl_arranged *s = dtfl_arranged_reduce_abelian(a, "Sum", i64, i64_diff,
    sum_logic, DTFL_NOCTX);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
.Fn dtfl_arranged_reduce_abelian
requires
.Va out_diff
to be Abelian
.Pq a negate operation ;
passing a non-Abelian difference class is a programming error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_collection_arrange 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_collection_join 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_collection_reduce 3 ,
.Xr dtfl-differential 7
.Sh HISTORY
Ported from differential-dataflow 0.25.1
.Pq Pa operators/arrange/arrangement.rs , Pa operators/reduce.rs , Pa collection.rs .
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
Every arrangement handle belongs to the worker that created it and must not
be used from another thread.
.Fn dtfl_collection_arrange_by_key
and the reduce operators build on that worker's dataflow.
